title: Blinder Tunnel ShelbyLoader Registry Run Persistence
id: 63ce815f-2750-4eb7-ac5f-e84039ee512d
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects creation of the HKCU Run value MicrosoftRuntime written by the
    ShelbyLoader V2 payload of the Iran-nexus Blinder Tunnel campaign
    (CL-STA-1178), which decrypts a Chisel tunneling configuration with the
    hard-coded RC4 key "My name is Blackwood !" and reverse-SOCKS proxies to
    port 10999. RuntimeBroker.dll or PsProxy.dll executed from non-standard
    paths corroborate the same intrusion.
references:
    - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/blinder-tunnel-targets-critical-infrastructure/
    - https://cyber.netsecops.io/articles/iranian-blinder-tunnel-campaign-targets-iraqi-critical-infrastructure/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-07
tags:
    - attack.t1547
logsource:
    category: registry_event
detection:
    selection_run_value:
        TargetObject|endswith:
            - '\CurrentVersion\Run\MicrosoftRuntime'
    condition: selection_run_value
falsepositives:
    - No legitimate application is known to create a Run value named MicrosoftRuntime; verify the image path before acting
level: high
